@startuml
title Two errors, two paths: a refusal of the business and a failing dependency
actor Customer as C
participant "Storefront" as SPA
participant "Web gateway" as GW
participant "Order service\ninbound adapter" as IN
participant "Use case\nand domain" as UC
participant "Cart and\ncatalog" as DEP

== a refusal: the cart changed since it was reviewed ==
C -> SPA : submits the checkout
SPA -> GW : POST /api/v1/orders
GW -> IN : forwards
IN -> UC : place the order
UC -> DEP : reads cart and prices
DEP --> UC : a price changed
UC --> IN : refusal "checkout outdated",\nwith the differences
note over IN : a result, not an exception:\nlogged as information, counted
IN --> SPA : 409, problem details,\ncode ERR-ORD-003, trace identifier
SPA --> C : "A price changed. Review your cart."\nthe differences, a reference

== a failure: the catalog does not answer ==
C -> SPA : submits the checkout
SPA -> GW : POST /api/v1/orders
GW -> IN : forwards
IN -> UC : place the order
UC -> DEP : reads prices
note over DEP #ECEFF1 : time limit reached,\ncircuit open
DEP --> UC : failure "catalog unavailable"
UC --> IN : failure of a dependency;\nnothing was created
note over IN : logged as a warning, counted;\nan alert watches the rate
IN --> SPA : 503, problem details,\ncode ERR-PLT-008, when to retry
SPA --> C : "We cannot take your order right now.\nNothing was charged. Try again in a moment."
@enduml
